"""d3zc_carry.py - CARRY-FORWARD exit ("until hit", up to 5 trading days) for the entries your d3z backtest already found.

Needs only what d3z saved: d3z_results/events.csv (stock, direction, date, entry type, entry minute). Yahoo and the stock-minute Dhan step are
NOT repeated. It only fetches option candles from Dhan (ATM + 3 strikes each side, entry day + the following days) and tests every
stop-loss / target pair with the trade kept open until hit.

  python d3zc_carry.py check | run | summary | range      (run is resumable, stops politely before the time budget)

Trade: ATM option at the entry minute (strike fixed at entry); SL 10/20 %, target 20..200 %; checked minute by minute across the next days
(entry day = day 1, max HOLD_DAYS = 5, never past the monthly expiry); overnight gap through the stop fills at the open ("STOP (gap)",
ret_pct = loss %); gap above target fills at the target; no hit by 15:30 of the last day = TIME exit.
Output: d3zc_results/ (parts, summaries, all_trades_combined/ = every trade in plain CSV).
"""
